iew": "robo man scare me, i like", "timestamp_created": 1719082120, "timestamp_updated": 1719082120, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "167937769", "author": {"steamid": "76561198068259101", "personaname": "jacky", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198068259101/", "num_games_owned": 231, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 2154, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1554, "deck_playtime_at_review": 29, "last_played": 1771832055, "avatar": "6ebdfa1cfbd3f50ce942485f178c415ad0999b58"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is one of the most slept-on games ever. Looking back on my time with this game, it was definitely some of the most fun I’ve ever had playing a video game. It’s like eating something really delicious or hearing a really good song (which this game has many of) that just makes your brain spray the good chemical. Super responsive controls, your character feels so snappy and mobile, game runs great so crank up the fps on a high refresh rate monitor and it’s a dream. If your main desire for a game is “satisfying gameplay” and not “character development” “story arc” or “next-gen graphics” (although the graphics have a borderlands-ish charm to them for sure) I can’t recommend Roboquest enough.", "timestamp_created": 1719078837, "timestamp_updated": 1719078837, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}]}